//! **Phase B, step three — the cost of the DERIVED chain.**
//!
//! `ir_lzb_cost` is the exact step count of one activation of the emitted
//! `Level::is_zero` body over `ir_lzb_module`, where the deref is an AUTHORED
//! seven-node model. `ir_lzd_cost` is the same function over `ir_lzd_module`,
//! where the deref is four of the compiler's own bodies — the kernel's
//! `<LevelArc as Deref>::deref`, and `as_deref`, `expect` and
//! `<Arc<Level>>::deref` as the callee sidecar derived them from their
//! monomorphized upstream MIR.
//!
//! ## The two functions differ in ONE constant, and it was measured
//!
//! Every deref frame costs `ir_d7` in `ir_lzb_cost` and `ir_d40` here. That 40
//! is not chosen and not counted by hand: it is SOLVED from three runs the
//! kernel computes, each of which exercises a different number of deref frames
//! and a different arm of the body —
//!
//! | witness                | arms                       | frames | steps |
//! |------------------------|----------------------------|--------|-------|
//! | `Max(Zero, Zero)`      | both operands read          | 2      | 107   |
//! | `Max(Succ(Zero), Zero)`| short circuit, second unread| 1      |  60   |
//! | `IMax(Zero, Zero)`     | switch default, first unread| 1      |  55   |
//!
//! `107 = 15 + 2D + 6 + 6`, `60 = 14 + D + 6`, `55 = 9 + D + 6` — three
//! equations, one unknown, and all three give `D = 40`. The non-deref constants
//! (15, 14, 9) are `ir_lzb_cost`'s own, unchanged, because the ROOT body is the
//! same emitted body in both modules.
//!
//! So this is a cost function whose every constant is either inherited from a
//! kernel-checked predecessor or over-determined by measurement, and the three
//! `*_is_*` pins below close the loop: they compute the function at the same
//! three Levels the machine was run at, so the cost FUNCTION and the cost
//! MEASUREMENT agree by two independent routes at every witness.
//!
//! ## A4 AND A5 ARE HERE
//!
//! This heading used to read "What is NOT here: A4 and A5 ... those are the next
//! step and nothing in this file claims them", and it stayed that way after the
//! step was taken. `SRC_IR_LZD_CORRECT` and `SRC_IR_LZD_MACHINE_SOUND`, ~110
//! lines below, are exactly A4 and A5 over `ir_lzd_module`, and the registration
//! comment on the first of them opens "*** A4 FOR THE DESIGNATED TARGET, OVER A
//! MODULE WITH NO AUTHORED FUNCTION IN IT. ***". A reader who trusted the
//! heading concluded the opposite of what the file does -- measured 2026-09-16,
//! when it sent a whole session's plan down the wrong branch.
//!
//! The three prerequisites the old text named are all present: the
//! representation relation is `EncodesLevelArcD` / `EncodesLiveLevelRefD`, its
//! frame lemma under the `as_deref` return-slot `alloca` is `ir_lzd_frame` /
//! `ir_lzd_frame_live`, and the activation induction is `ir_lzd_activation` with
//! its `max_false` / `max_true` / `imax` segment lemmas.
//!
//! ## What genuinely remains
//!
//! Two LAYOUT obligations the artifact does not prove, both carried by the
//! representation relation and both the same class as the `a+8`/`a+16` offsets
//! and the 16-byte `ArcInner` header `ir_lzb_correct` already carries:
//!
//! * a live `Arc` pointer is never the zero word (the niche -- structural,
//!   because `Option<Arc<Level>>` is niche-encoded);
//! * every represented address is below the allocation counter (freshness --
//!   which is what an allocation counter means).
//!
//! What is GONE is the authored function: `ir_lzb_deref` was link 4's residual
//! for the designated target and this module does not contain it.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

